# PM-32 (design §15.7) on the recipient's side: a recipient that, when the KEM key does not open
# the inner layer, retries with a key without the X-Wing secret — the all-zero one, which PQ5's
# gate-variant client uses. Honest senders are unaffected (one decapsulation per open, and a
# perturbed secret fails both keys), so only a sender that sealed without the KEM tells: PQ5's gate
# variant is accepted, and PQ1's one inner key per open refuses the retry on the gate envelopes.
# kills: pq_bump::pq1_every_intro_of_the_world_opens_through_the_host_open_intro_body_under_the_assertion
# kills: pq_bump::pq1_every_intro_open_of_the_world_decapsulates_exactly_once
# kills: pq_bump::pq1_the_host_assertion_passes_every_open_of_the_world
